@model ReformedHistory.Views.Content.Confessions.Secret.SecretSection

<h2 id="@this.Model.Link">Chapter @this.Model.Index</h2>
<h3>@this.Model.Name</h3>
<br />

<div class="centerQuote">
    <span>
        For He chose us, not because we believed, but that we might believe.
    </span>
    <span>Saint Augustine, On the Predestination of the Saints</span>
</div>
    
<ol>
    <li>
        The Lord is God Almighty, the beginning and the end, the timeless and immutable creator of the world, who
        made all things that exist in heaven and on earth from nothing by the Word of His power.
        <!--<a href="#MajestyOfGod.Sources.1">(@(this.Model.Index).1)</a>.-->
    </li>
    <!--<li>
        By the most wise and holy counsel of his own will, God freely and unchangeably ordains whatsoever comes 
        to pass. However, this is done in such a way so that God is the author of sin, nor is violence offered to the will of 
        the creatures; nor is the liberty of second causes taken away, but rather established.
    </li>-->
    @*<li>
        Before the very foundation of the world, while nobody had yet done anything good or evil,
        God predestined a people for His own possession:
        a holy nation, a royal priesthood, to be adopted as sons of God in Christ Jesus,
        being called out of darkness and cleansed of all their sins to receive the inheritance of eternal life.
        <!--<a href="#MajestyOfGod.Sources.2">(@(this.Model.Index).2)</a>.-->
    </li>*@
    <li>
        Before the very foundation of the world, while nobody had yet done anything good or evil, God
        predestined a people for Himself, that they would be the inheritors of eternal life in Christ.
    </li>
    <li>
        This decree of predestination is not based on foreseen faith or merit of any kind, but 
        is purely one of gracious, undeserved love. 
        
        Even in those who believe, faith is a gift from God and cannot be obtained through human effort.
        
        For as Saint Paul teaches, none may boast except 
        in the kindness and mercy of God, who for His own sake determined to save sinners from their
        rebellion.
    </li>
    <li>
        God knows each of His predestined people by name, and nothing on heaven or earth can pluck them from His hand.
    </li>
</ol>
<br />